;; Is there a procedure worth keeping in the turns since the last judgement?
;; brainyard's `SkillDistillationBatch` (common/skill_distill/signatures.clj),
;; word for word, and the port's only distiller (RFC-017).
;;
;; brainyard also has `SkillDistillation`, which judges one turn, for its
;; :per-turn mode. Here a window of one turn (:skill-distill-judge-window 1)
;; is still a window, so one predictor serves every case (divergence
;; `one-distiller-for-every-window`).
;;
;; The session tree runs it (loops/session.edn, :session/distill-window) over the
;; candidate turns not yet judged — those that answered in two or more tool
;; calls. It runs as soon as those turns show a procedure (a tool sequence
;; repeated, or one long one), at the latest every :skill-distill-judge-window
;; turns, and once more when the session ends, over whatever is left. What it drafts is
;; STAGED under .brainyard/skills/proposals for a person to accept.
{:id "session/distill-skill"
 :strategy :cot
 :description "Find the single best reusable procedure in a window of recent turns, and draft the skill if there is one."
 :instructions "You judge whether a WINDOW of recent agent turns contains a NOVEL, REUSABLE
procedure worth saving as a skill, and if so you draft the skill.

The window holds several turns that each already passed a cheap filter (they
succeeded and took multiple action steps). Read them together. A procedure is
worth saving ONLY when ALL hold:
- It is GENERALIZABLE and multi-step — a recipe, not a one-off answer, a single
  edit, or a lookup.
- It would plausibly REPEAT on a similar future task.
- No skill in `existing-skills` already covers it (do not duplicate).

Look ACROSS turns, not only within them: a procedure that was carried out over
two or three consecutive turns (investigate → change → verify) is exactly what
this batch view is for, and is often stronger than anything a single turn shows.

Return the single BEST candidate in the window. Most windows contain none —
return :reusable false with a low :score and an empty :skill-md when in doubt.
A weak or speculative skill is worse than none.

When (and only when) the window IS skill-worthy:
- :reusable     true
- :score        your confidence 0.0..1.0 (the caller stages a proposal only
                past a configured threshold)
- :proposed-name  lowercase-kebab, leading letter (^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$), short
                  and descriptive; must not collide with an existing skill
- :rationale    one or two sentences: what the reusable procedure is, and which
                turns it came from
- :skill-md     a COMPLETE SKILL.md document: YAML front-matter (name,
                description) followed by a concise, imperative how-to distilled
                from the ACTUAL steps in the window — the tool sequence, the
                order, the decision points, and any pitfall the turns hit. Write
                it as instructions for next time, not a narration of what
                happened. No secrets, no machine-specific absolute paths, no
                one-off data.

When NOT skill-worthy: :reusable false, :score low, :proposed-name \"\",
:rationale one line on why nothing in the window generalizes, :skill-md \"\"."
 :inputs
 [[:turn-window {:desc "Several recent turns, each headed by its turn number and question, followed by its compacted iteration trace"} :string]
  [:turn-count {:desc "How many turns the window holds"} :string]
  [:existing-skills {:desc "Existing skill names + one-line descriptions, one per line — do NOT duplicate any of these"} :string]
  [:project-context {:desc "Optional one-line project context (or empty)"} :string]]
 :outputs
 [[:reusable {:desc "True only when the window contains a novel, generalizable, repeatable procedure not already covered"} :boolean]
  [:score {:desc "0.0..1.0 — confidence this turn is a novel reusable procedure worth a skill"} [:double {:min 0.0 :max 1.0}]]
  [:proposed-name {:desc "Proposed skill name: lowercase-kebab, leading letter, ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$ (empty when not reusable)"} :string]
  [:rationale {:desc "One or two sentences on the reusable procedure and which turns it came from (or why nothing generalizes)"} :string]
  [:skill-md {:desc "Complete SKILL.md draft (front-matter + imperative how-to) when reusable; empty string otherwise"} :string]]}
